lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix committed as 83ca81e709e (worktree win-ctypes-trim): `_malloc_trim()` returns None when `sys.platform` is not Linux. Evidence before push:\n- New test `test_windows_has_no_trim_and_a_release_does_not_raise` fails on origin/main 57d45053272 with `TypeError: LoadLibrary() argument 1 must be str, not None`; passes with the fix (file: 4 passed, 1 skipped on macOS).\n- With `ctypes.CDLL(None)` patched to raise that TypeError, the 16 files from job 133771119760: 47 failed on origin/main (superset of all 46 Windows failures); 318 passed, 0 failed with the fix.\n`make verify` running now; push to Gerrit follows.","timestamp":1794888143341053337}],"created_at":1794887238660630282,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b77a52ca-00be-4ec3-a38a-f850582d0911","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"e152-4009-4180-4fd8"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nChange 3407 (merged as 9beecb409ab, bug unmedical-stational-chrysalis) made the MCP in-flight gauge call `release_freed_heap()` when its count returns to zero. `_malloc_trim()` (`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:68`) resolves glibc's `malloc_trim` with `ctypes.CDLL(None)` and catches only `AttributeError` and `OSError`. On Windows, `ctypes.CDLL(None)` raises `TypeError: LoadLibrary() argument 1 must be str, not None`, so every release that takes the gauge to zero raises. That breaks every certified/signing tool call (`transition_ticket`, `verify_completion`, `review_plan`, `sign_manifest`, `sign_review`) and every direct gauge release on Windows.\n\n## Observation\n\n- GitHub Actions run 44002909290, job 133771119760 (\"sweep (windows)\", main at 390f926c7ea): 46 failures, all in MCP tests; the log contains 109 lines with `LoadLibrary() argument 1 must be str, not None`.\n- Reproduced on macOS by patching `ctypes.CDLL` so `CDLL(None)` raises that `TypeError`: running the 16 affected test files on origin/main 57d45053272 gives 47 failures, a superset of all 46 Windows failures (including the parity `REJECTED`-vs-`ACCEPTED` cases and the missing `signed_at` case, which receive the `TypeError` as a failed tool call). The one extra, `test_close_picked_up_but_not_started_when_the_server_stops_never_runs`, does not run in the Windows sweep.\n\n## Approach\n\nMake `_malloc_trim()` return `None` on any platform that is not Linux, before touching `ctypes` (`sys.platform.startswith(\"linux\")`), and keep the existing `AttributeError`/`OSError` catch for Linux C libraries without `malloc_trim` (musl). glibc is a Linux C library, so no other platform can have `malloc_trim`. No config key, environment variable, flag or other mechanism.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py`: platform check in `_malloc_trim()`; docstring states the Windows case.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_heap_release.py`: Windows-shaped test.\n\n## Testing\n\n- New test: with `sys.platform` set to `win32`, `ctypes.CDLL(None)` patched to raise `TypeError` as on Windows, and the `_malloc_trim` cache cleared, `release_freed_heap()` returns `False` and a gauge `hold()` release does not raise. It fails on current main (the `TypeError` escapes) and passes with the fix.\n- Re-run the 16 affected files under the same `ctypes.CDLL(None)` simulation: 0 failures expected.\n- Existing Linux tests keep passing (`release_freed_heap()` is `True` on Linux; the idle-memory test still releases memory).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `_malloc_trim()` returns `None` without calling `ctypes.CDLL` on non-Linux platforms, and `pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_heap_release.py` passes.\n- [ ] The new Windows-shaped test fails on origin/main 57d45053272 and passes with the fix.\n- [ ] Under the `ctypes.CDLL(None)`-raises-`TypeError` simulation, the 16 test files that failed in job 133771119760 report 0 failures.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes, and `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] After merge, a dispatched `test.yml` run on main has its \"sweep (windows)\" job pass; the run and job IDs are recorded here.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_health.py","reason":"_malloc_trim returns None off Linux instead of calling ctypes.CDLL(None)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_heap_release.py","reason":"Windows-shaped regression test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c966a19e-ed2c-4ed6-bc58-80428f97e8cb","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["mcp","windows"],"ticket_id":"6238-9307-c74c-4d5c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP certified and signing tools fail on Windows: the idle heap trim calls ctypes.CDLL(None), which raises TypeError there","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d401512f-5253-4e19-8718-4ed6c2488bf3","b77a52ca-00be-4ec3-a38a-f850582d0911","d7df4949-dbc8-4cf2-9025-42f7afd10595","c5f49ccd-9072-4f5a-ac50-54f341feb567","c966a19e-ed2c-4ed6-bc58-80428f97e8cb","a4bf250b-a75f-4612-9c62-07ae19ff7df1","85a15705-c710-43c4-b43f-584b3c084676"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794888143341053338,"uuid":"e5ce1cde-2d4f-459c-92c9-48844492ba1a"}
